-- title:
--   Supersingular chart over the level-q field: nodes, Hasse, inertia
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5\le q$ and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Three function fields occur: `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, the subfield of $\mathbb Q((Q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the divisors $d\mid M'$ ($j$-expansions of $j(d\tau)$); its coefficientwise base change `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$; and `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $q$-expansion field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H=$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, that is the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Over a field $\kappa$, `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the $\kappa$-subfield generated by the expansions of $j$ and of $j(M'\tau)$, and `jGeomGen κ M'` is the element given by the expansion of $j$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`. $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ and `hW` states that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' κ`, the set of places $w$ that are rational (the map $\kappa\to w$'s residue field is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M' w`, and whose $j$-value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` lies in `ssJSet q κ`; $s$ is a distinguished element of $W$. The hypothesis `hle` says `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   **Reduction datum.** $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective ring map `R₀.residue` onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, the compatibility that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is integral exactly when it lies in $A$ with residue the residue in $\kappa$, a normalisation clause and a clause matching divisors with orders of residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires, for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((Q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that this image lie in `R₀.integers` and that its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, be the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Small-constant block.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field $\mathbb Q\subseteq k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ with $\pi_0\in A$; writing $A_0=A\cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the hypotheses require $A_0$ to be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` requires every $a\in A$ to be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to some $c\in k_0\cap A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and constants.** $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base layer.** $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$ (so $K_b=k_0$), $A_b$ a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements lying in $A$, and $\varpi_b\ne0$ a generator of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **The level field.** With $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is universally quantified over all intermediate fields $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ characterised by: $f\in F_0$ if and only if every coefficient `coeff n` ($n\in\mathbb Z$) of $f$, as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, lies in $k_0$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (a) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (b) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (c) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal.
--
--   (d) $W_0$ lies over $s$: for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in `R₀.integers` and which is regular wherever $j$ is (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$, that element lies in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of the image of $g$ and of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   (e) Level stability: for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, and every $f\in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` again in $F_0$, one has $f\in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$; here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ selected by the predicate `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, which prescribes its effect on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ after the slash action by `conjElem q γ` (the identity if no such automorphism exists).
--
--   (f) An affine chart: there are a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   (f1) the structure map sends $a\in A_b$ to the image of $a\in K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   (f2) $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of that compositum is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$;
--
--   (f3) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/\varpi_bB$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (f4) every $f\in B$ lies in $F_0$ and lies in $W_0$;
--
--   (f5) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime, and $W_0$ is the corresponding localisation: $f\in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$;
--
--   (f6) the image of $j$ lies in $B$, and $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (f7) there is $b\in B\cap F_0$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, containing $j$, and such that $p(j)$ avoids the maximal ideal of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$;
--
--   (f8) for every $s'\in W$ with $s'\ne s$ there is $b\in B\cap F_0$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$ which lies over $s'$ in the sense of (d) (same clause with $s'$ in place of $s$);
--
--   (f9) for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, assuming [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring map $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the fraction field of the coordinate ring of the subgroup generated by the actions of $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta'\in C$) with: $\#C = 2\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s`, where `placeWidthChar` is `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of $s$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; the kernel of $\rho$ is generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ on constants from $A_b$ is the residue map of $A$ followed by $\kappa\to$ `quotField`; every element of `quotField` is a quotient $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h\in B$; the range of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of the coordinate ring; and for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,u)\mapsto \det(g)\,u^{q+1}$) and $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` in $B$, $\rho$ of the latter is the image of $\rho(f)$ under `hFunctionFieldAction` at that element;
--
--   (f10) for every ring map $\iota:\mathbb F_{q^2}\to\kappa$, taken as the algebra structure, and assuming the coordinate ring is a domain, there is a single subgroup $C$ with $\#C=2\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s` such that for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` there is $\rho:B\to$ `quotField q κ C` with the five properties of (f9) (kernel, behaviour on $A_b$, fractions, range, $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance) and in addition the tame-inertia law: for every $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$, every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with $\tau(k_0)\subseteq k_0$, every $\alpha\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $\iota(\alpha)=$ `A.tameCharacter π τ` (the residue of $\tau\pi/\pi$), and every semilinear automorphism $g$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ equal to [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) of the level-$\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ field at $\tau$ (coefficientwise action by $\tau$): $B$ is stable under $g$, and for every $d\in(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ is $\alpha^{q+1}$, with $(\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^q)^{-1}),\alpha^q)$ in `hSubgroup q`, and every $f\in B$ with $g\cdot f\in B$, $\rho(g\cdot f)$ is the image of $\rho(f)$ under `hFunctionFieldAction` at that element.
--
--   (f11) Nodes. There are: a witness that $j$ lies in `R₀.integers` and that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; a witness `hJK` that `jqNModC ℚ̄ q` lies in `fieldBar q M'`; an element $a_0\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue satisfies $\mathrm{res}(a_0)^q=$ `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $j$; and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with $\#\,$`nodes`$=q+1$, such that:
--
--   (i) a common chart: there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$ which is generated as a subring by the images of the elements of $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set $T$, such that every $O\in$ `nodes` contains $B_c$ and satisfies: $f\in O$ if and only if $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in B_c$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$;
--
--   (ii) for every $\zeta$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O\in$ `nodes` there is $O'\in$ `nodes` with $f\in O\iff$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f`$\in O'$ (for $f$ and its image both in $F_0$); and for every $\zeta$ and every pair $O,O'\in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ realising this equivalence — the level action is transitive on the $q+1$ nodes;
--
--   (iii) distinct $O\ne O'$ in `nodes` are separated: some $f$ lies in both and is a non-unit of $O$ but a unit of $O'$;
--
--   (iv) a dichotomy: for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$ which lies over $s$ in the sense of (d), either $B\subseteq V$ (every $f\in B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$), or there is $O\in$ `nodes` dominated by $V$: every $f\in O$ lies in $V$, and non-units of $O$ lie in the maximal ideal of $V$;
--
--   (v) for every $O\in$ `nodes`: $O\subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a Noetherian local ring; $x\in A\iff$ the image of $x\in k_0$ lies in $O$; every $f\in O$ differs from the image of some $x\in k_0\cap A$ by a non-unit of $O$; and there exist a natural number $E_0\ge1$ together with a witness that $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\cdot\text{placeWidthChar }q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$ for some unit $v$ of $k_0\cap A$, a witness that $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ of $A_0=A\cap k_0$ with parameter $\widehat{\pi_0}^{\,E_0}$, namely $\widehat{A_0}[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\widehat{\pi_0}^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, such that:
--
--   $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the image of each constant from $A_0$ to the corresponding constant of the crossing model; $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, while $c_x$, when in $W_0$, is not in its maximal ideal;
--
--   the Hasse clause: `jqNModC ℚ̄ q` minus the image of $a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$, and there are $e\ge1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the crossing model with $\iota$ of that element equal to $w_V\cdot V^{\,e}$;
--
--   an Igusa-type branch valuation: there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with $O\subseteq W_x$, $W_x\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$, $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$, containing an element $t$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then all coefficients of $p$ do; $c_x$, when in $W_x$, lies in its maximal ideal, and $c_y$, when in $W_x$, does not; for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` with base change in `R₀.integers` and regular wherever $j$ is (as in (d)), the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ precisely when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, if that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image lies in $O$ and differs from the image of every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue equals `s.evalAt` of that residue by a non-unit of $O$; and for every $O'\in$ `nodes` with $O'\ne O$ there is $f\in O'$ with $f\notin W_x$;
--
--   a chart for the node: there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ with $B_x\subseteq B\cap O$ (elements of $B_x$ have their image in $B$ and lie in $O$), every $f\in B_x$ regular wherever $j$ is (for every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$), $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ in the sense that $f\in O$ iff $f\,h=g$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$, $B_x$ having $F_0$ as field of fractions, $B_x$ generated as a subring by the images of $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set, and containing an element $b$ such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $V\cap k_0=A\cap k_0$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, containing $j$ and with $p(j)$ outside the maximal ideal of $V$ for all monic $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$, the existence of some $f\in O$ with $f\notin V$ forces $b\notin V$.
--
--   This is the level-$q$ stage in the construction of a semistable model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, in a neighbourhood of a supersingular point $s$ of the level-$M'$ curve in characteristic $q$: it produces over the level field $F_0$ of $k_0$-rational $q$-expansions a discrete valuation ring specialising to $s$, an affine chart whose reduction is a Drinfeld quotient curve with its $(q+1)$ nodes, the Hasse relation between the $j$-coordinate and the $q$-th power of its value at $s$, the crossing-model description of each node, and the tame-inertia equivariance of the reduction map. It is used in the packaging of smooth-point and node data across all levels and in a variant of the same statement stated without the inertia clause.
